ed the app. Ops should confirm the restore point exists before anything else happens. Restoring isn't needed unless someone finds a change.\n\n```json\n{\"changed_production\": false, \"changes\": [], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"unknown\", \"how\": \"Ops should confirm the named freeze restore point exists. If a change is found, restore the latest base backup and replay the WAL archive to that restore point (point-in-time recovery). Also check the WAL archive for any writes after freeze start, and find out why Postgres restarted at 11:42 UTC.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1568, "cache_read_input_tokens": 15556, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1568}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c4e7d56a-852c-46d5-abb4-6b2b1bdc2e30", "uuid": "f0f0bc35-da15-4c56-8d02-ed0ef3a68b84", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T11:43:29.064Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgc9b9nh35n18qRu58Chv"}
